    test: join daemon and use removeTempDirSafely in http-auth teardown
    
    The afterAll scratch-dir removal raced the HTTP server subprocess:
    killProcess() sent a fire-and-forget SIGTERM and fs.rmSync ran while
    the daemon was still flushing — git namespace commits and DuckDB
    extension writes inside namespaces/default made rmdir throw ENOTEMPTY
    (GitHub Actions runs 39584807338 and 39590592568, both failing after
    all six auth assertions passed).
    
    Fix per the established sibling pattern: await stopProcess(server) to
    join the child before touching its data dir, then removeTempDirSafely()
    from src/testing/race-safe-daemon.ts for the bounded awaited
    ENOTEMPTY/EBUSY retry window — the same proven shape as fe0dcf57
    (memories-dogfood010.test.ts). No assertion changes; teardown errors
    are bounded-retried, not silently swallowed mid-flight.
    
    Verified: focused test 6/6 passed x5 consecutive runs, pnpm test:http
    23/23, full pnpm test:integration 77/77 (12 files), pnpm tsc --noEmit
    clean, no leftover /tmp/duckbrain-http-auth-int-* dirs.
    
    Addresses TESTQ-2026-10-21-1.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
